The src/pscf directory contains source files for classes and functions that
are defined in the Pscf C++ namespace and that can be used by any program 
in the PSCF package.  

Subdirectories:
---------------

   chem/         - molecular structure descriptors
   correlation/  - correlation functions for homogeneous gas
   cuda/         - utilities and cufft complex type for GPUs
   cpu/          - utilities that use FFTW complex type for CPUs
   environment/  - generation of imposed mask and external fields
   floryHuggins/ - Flory-Huggins theory for homogeneous mixtures
   inter/        - interaction (excess) free energy 
   iterator/     - utilities for iterator algorithms
   math/         - mathematical utilities
   mesh/         - spatial mesh and mesh iterators
   solvers/      - templates for modified diffusion eqn (MDE) solvers 
   sweep/        - utilities for SCFT sweep algorithms
   tests/        - unit tests for code in src/pscf

   Most named entitites in the src/pscf directory are defined directly
   in the top-level Pscf namespace. The most important exceptions are:

   - All classes in subdirectory pscf/floryHuggins are defined in a 
     nested namespace named Pscf::FloryHuggins. 
 
   - All classes and functions in subdirectory pscf/correlation are 
     defined in a nested namespace named Pscf::Correlation

C++ file:
---------

paths.h  - directory paths used by C++ files (installed by configure script)

Makefile and makefile fragments:
--------------------------------

makefile     - main makefile for src/pscf directory tree
sources.mk   - list of source files in src/pscf (makefile fragment)
patterns.mk  - pattern rules for use in src/pscf (makefile fragment)

